slimserve: glm53f-q2-1 is not ready on Apple Silicon (Metal): single-stream serving is qualified; concurrent serving scales but has not met the batching bar (>= 2x at c=4, >= 3x at c=16). Every pinned exact-token gate is concurrency 1 and passes bit-identically (8tok 7dd30ea193a6, off1-2000 393882a2ddaf, 2500x64 1d7d58486dc7) at 34-40 tok/s decode and 237-258 t/s prefill, beating ds4 on the same box by ~1.5x and ~1.8x. Concurrent serving (batching campaign, 2026-09-17): 1000-token prompts / 400 output tokens aggregate 25.8 / 33.2 / 35.8 / 40.0 / 42.9 tok/s at c=1/2/4/8/16 (1.29 / 1.39 / 1.56 / 1.67x); decode-dominated (1000 output tokens) 1.88x at c=8 and 2.08x at c=16. The bar is >= 2x at c=4 and >= 3x at c=16; the record stays gated until it is met and concurrent gates are pinned. SLIMSERVE_SERVE_IN_PROGRESS=1 boots it meanwhile. Continuing: SLIMSERVE_SERVE_IN_PROGRESS=1.
